[ext_resource type="Resource" path="res://resources/tiles/road_banked_right.tres" id="2_profile"]

; A quarter turn to the right of 63 m radius — the catalog's CornerRadius, and the number the
; profile's 60-degree lip was written against: a bank holds a car unaided at
; v = sqrt(g * r * tan(theta)), which at 2 g and these two lands neutral just under TopSpeed.
;
; The arc is one cubic Bezier. Two control points with handles of 4/3 * tan(45/2) * r = 34.794 m
; reproduce a quarter circle to well under a centimetre, which is far inside the width of the
; paint. Entry sits at the origin heading -Z and the exit lands at (63, 0, -63) heading +X, which
; is exactly what TrackAnchor.Swept folds onto the head for a right-hand quarter turn.
[sub_resource type="Curve3D" id="Curve_right"]
